```python
regression(
    data,
    y,
    x,
    year=None,
    *,
    fixed_effects=None,
    cluster=None,
    robust=True,
    title=None,
    ref=None,
)
```

Ordinary least squares, with several specifications side by side.

## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}

| Name          | Type        | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | Default    |
|---------------|-------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|
| data          |             | A dataset id, or a panel with ``geo_id`` (and ``year``), e.g. from ``load`` or ``combine``                                                                                                                                                                           | _required_ |
| y             | str         | The outcome column                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | _required_ |
| x             |             | The regressors: a column or a list of columns (one model), or a list of lists (one model per list, e.g. adding controls step by step)                                                                                                                                | _required_ |
| year          |             | The year to use (default: the last with data for ``y`` and every regressor), a list of years, or ``"all"`` to pool every year                                                                                                                                        | `None`     |
| fixed_effects |             | A column, a coarser scale (e.g. the scale above the units'), ``"year"``, or a list of them: absorbed as dummies and reported as Yes/No rows instead of coefficients. A list with one entry per model, where an entry is ``None`` or a list, sets them model by model | `None`     |
| cluster       | str \| None | A column or a coarser scale: standard errors clustered by it (p-values and intervals then use a t distribution with one degree of freedom less than clusters)                                                                                                        | `None`     |
| robust        | bool        | Heteroskedasticity-robust standard errors (HC1) when there is no ``cluster``; ``False``: classical standard errors                                                                                                                                                   | `True`     |
| title         | str \| None | The title of the table and of the figure                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | `None`     |

## Returns {.doc-section .doc-section-returns}

| Name   | Type             | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |
|--------|------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | RegressionResult | A result with ``.gt`` (the regression table: coefficients with stars, standard errors in parentheses, the fixed effects, N and R²), ``.fig`` (the coefficients with 95% confidence intervals across models), ``.df`` (tidy: ``model``, ``term``, ``estimate``, ``std_error``, ``statistic``, ``p_value``, ``conf_low``, ``conf_high``), ``.summary`` (one row per model: ``n``, ``r2``, ``r2_adj``, ``fixed_effects``, ``std_errors``), ``.models`` (the fitted statsmodels results) and ``.interpret()``. |

## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}

```python
!pip install -q geo4bolivia
import geo4bolivia as geo

res = geo.regression("sdg", "index_sdg",
                     [["urbanization"], ["urbanization", "population"]],
                     fixed_effects=[None, "department"])
print(res.interpret())
res.gt
```


